# Quick Start

Welcome to the Codexeron Quick Start Guide.

This guide will help you make your first successful request to the Codexeron API in just a few minutes.

---

# Before You Begin

Before continuing, make sure you have completed the following steps:

- Installed PHP 8.3 or later
- Installed Composer
- Created a Codexeron account
- Generated an API Key
- Completed the Configuration guide

---

# Step 1 — Get Your API Key

Sign in to your Codexeron account.

Navigate to:

Developer Dashboard → API Keys

Create a new API Key and store it securely.

Never share your API Key publicly.

---

# Step 2 — Configure Your Environment

Example environment variables:

```env
CODEXERON_API_URL=https://api.codexeron.com
CODEXERON_API_KEY=your_api_key
```

---

# Step 3 — Your First API Request

Example request:

```http
GET /v1/products
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY
Accept: application/json
```

---

# Example Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Example Product"
    }
  ]
}
```

---

# Step 4 — Handle Errors

Always validate the response before processing data.

Common HTTP status codes:

| Code | Description |
|------|-------------|
| 200 | Success |
| 201 | Resource Created |
| 400 | Bad Request |
| 401 | Unauthorized |
| 403 | Forbidden |
| 404 | Not Found |
| 429 | Too Many Requests |
| 500 | Internal Server Error |

---

# Best Practices

For the best experience:

- Store API Keys securely.
- Always use HTTPS.
- Validate API responses.
- Handle exceptions correctly.
- Respect API rate limits.
- Keep your dependencies updated.

